# oneTBB scheduler/partitioner reports from parallel_for_each -- internal
# TSan races inside TBB's own scheduler bookkeeping, not naja-owned data.
# These are read via tsan-build.yml's ctest step
# (TSAN_OPTIONS=...suppressions=.github/tsan.supp), which relies on
# ctest simply inheriting the job's environment -- no special plumbing
# needed there. Patterns are bare substring matches (no wildcards
# required for TSan's suppression matcher to apply them); wrapped in
# leading/trailing '*' here defensively, which is harmless but not
# functionally required.
race:*tbb::detail::d1::dynamic_grainsize_mode*
race:*tbb::detail::d1::adaptive_mode*
race:*tbb::detail::d1::start_for*

# oneTBB's fold_tree/partitioner ref-count bookkeeping racing against its
# own concurrent_unordered_set insert path -- same scheduler-internal noise
# as above, just a different pair of frames (both inside TBB, unrelated to
# any naja-owned data: see LoadlessLogicRemover::getTracedIsos, which only
# ever inserts into each thread's own tracedIsos.local() before merging
# serially). Only reproduces when the MT path is active (this workflow's
# NON_MT=1 keeps RemoveLoadlessLogic.cpp/DNL_impl.h/LogicCone.cpp off this
# path entirely) and enough hierarchy/instances exist to spin up multiple
# TBB workers, as simple_2_loadless_3_levels does.
race:*tbb::detail::d1::concurrent_unordered_base*
race:*tbb::detail::d1::fold_tree*
